 "kind": "transient",
 "story": "A temperature sensor's voltage drifts slowly up and down between 0 and 5 V (here a 1 Hz sine centred on 2.5 V). A comparator (an op-amp with no feedback, powered from 0 and 5 V) must switch its output HIGH whenever the sensor is above 2.0 V and LOW below it. The reference comes from a divider on the 5 V rail: the bottom resistor is 10 kOhm, you choose the top one.",
